hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1062","Ours is Muhammad bin Yahya, Abu Hatim Al-Razi, Saeed bin Muhammad bin Thawab Al-Husri Al-Basri, and Al-Abbas bin Yazid Al-Bahrani, They said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abi Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “took the tashahhud in the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and said hello.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Hatim, which he told us in Basra. He praised him in Baghdad once, and said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed with them, but he made a mistake, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after greeting and speaking.” As for Muhammad ibn Yahya, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed with them, but he missed it in his prayer, so he prostrated two prostrations, then he recited the tashahhud, then He said hello. Saeed bin Muhammad said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with them, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he recited the tashahhud and said the salutations. Abu Bakr said: I did not give a word other than Al-Abbas."
